  25:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****   ==============================================================================
  26:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****                         ##### How to use this driver #####
  27:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****   ==============================================================================
  28:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****   [..]
  29:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     The UART HAL driver can be used as follows:
  30:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  31:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Declare a UART_HandleTypeDef handle structure (eg. UART_HandleTypeDef huart).
  32:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Initialize the UART low level resources by implementing the HAL_UART_MspInit() API:
  33:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (##) Enable the USARTx interface clock.
  34:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (##) UART pins configuration:
  35:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Enable the clock for the UART GPIOs.
  36:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Configure the UART TX/RX pins as alternate function pull-up.
  37:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (##) NVIC configuration if you need to use interrupt process (HAL_UART_Transmit_IT()
  38:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****              and HAL_UART_Receive_IT() APIs):
  39:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Configure the USARTx interrupt priority.
  40:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Enable the NVIC USART IRQ handle.
  41:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (##) DMA Configuration if you need to use DMA process (HAL_UART_Transmit_DMA()
  42:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****              and HAL_UART_Receive_DMA() APIs):
  43:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Declare a DMA handle structure for the Tx/Rx stream.
  44:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Enable the DMAx interface clock.
  45:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Configure the declared DMA handle structure with the required
  46:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****                   Tx/Rx parameters.
  47:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Configure the DMA Tx/Rx stream.
  48:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Associate the initialized DMA handle to the UART DMA Tx/Rx handle.
  49:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Configure the priority and enable the NVIC for the transfer complete
  50:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****                   interrupt on the DMA Tx/Rx stream.
  51:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             (+++) Configure the USARTx interrupt priority and enable the NVIC USART IRQ handle
  52:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****                   (used for last byte sending completion detection in DMA non circular mode)
  53:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  54:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Program the Baud Rate, Word Length, Stop Bit, Parity, Hardware
  55:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         flow control and Mode(Receiver/Transmitter) in the huart Init structure.
  56:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  57:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) For the UART asynchronous mode, initialize the UART registers by calling
  58:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         the HAL_UART_Init() API.
  59:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  60:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) For the UART Half duplex mode, initialize the UART registers by calling
  61:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         the HAL_HalfDuplex_Init() API.
  62:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  63:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) For the LIN mode, initialize the UART registers by calling the HAL_LIN_Init() API.
  64:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  65:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) For the Multi-Processor mode, initialize the UART registers by calling
  66:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         the HAL_MultiProcessor_Init() API.
  67:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  68:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
  69:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (@) The specific UART interrupts (Transmission complete interrupt,
  70:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             RXNE interrupt and Error Interrupts) will be managed using the macros
  71:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             __HAL_UART_ENABLE_IT() and __HAL_UART_DISABLE_IT() inside the transmit
  72:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             and receive process.
  73:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  74:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
  75:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (@) These APIs (HAL_UART_Init() and HAL_HalfDuplex_Init()) configure also the
  76:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             low level Hardware GPIO, CLOCK, CORTEX...etc) by calling the customized
  77:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             HAL_UART_MspInit() API.
  78:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  79:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     ##### Callback registration #####
  80:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     ==================================
  81:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  82:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
  83:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     The compilation define USE_HAL_UART_REGISTER_CALLBACKS when set to 1
  84:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     allows the user to configure dynamically the driver callbacks.
  85:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
  86:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
  87:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     Use Function HAL_UART_RegisterCallback() to register a user callback.
  88:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     Function HAL_UART_RegisterCallback() allows to register following callbacks:
  89:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) TxHalfCpltCallback        : Tx Half Complete Callback.
  90:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) TxCpltCallback            : Tx Complete Callback.
  91:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) RxHalfCpltCallback        : Rx Half Complete Callback.
  92:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) RxCpltCallback            : Rx Complete Callback.
  93:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback             : Error Callback.
  94:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) AbortCpltCallback         : Abort Complete Callback.
  95:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) AbortTransmitCpltCallback : Abort Transmit Complete Callback.
  96:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) AbortReceiveCpltCallback  : Abort Receive Complete Callback.
  97:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback           : UART MspInit.
  98:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback         : UART MspDeInit.
  99:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     This function takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle, the Callback ID
 100:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     and a pointer to the user callback function.
 101:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 102:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
 103:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     Use function HAL_UART_UnRegisterCallback() to reset a callback to the default
 104:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     weak (surcharged) function.
 105:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     HAL_UART_UnRegisterCallback() takes as parameters the HAL peripheral handle,
 106:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     and the Callback ID.
 107:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     This function allows to reset following callbacks:
 108:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) TxHalfCpltCallback        : Tx Half Complete Callback.
 109:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) TxCpltCallback            : Tx Complete Callback.
 110:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) RxHalfCpltCallback        : Rx Half Complete Callback.
 111:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) RxCpltCallback            : Rx Complete Callback.
 112:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) ErrorCallback             : Error Callback.
 113:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) AbortCpltCallback         : Abort Complete Callback.
 114:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) AbortTransmitCpltCallback : Abort Transmit Complete Callback.
 115:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) AbortReceiveCpltCallback  : Abort Receive Complete Callback.
 116:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) MspInitCallback           : UART MspInit.
 117:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (+) MspDeInitCallback         : UART MspDeInit.
 118:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 119:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
 120:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     For specific callback RxEventCallback, use dedicated registration/reset functions:
 121:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     respectively HAL_UART_RegisterRxEventCallback() , HAL_UART_UnRegisterRxEventCallback().
 122:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 123:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
 124:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     By default, after the HAL_UART_Init() and when the state is HAL_UART_STATE_RESET
 125:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     all callbacks are set to the corresponding weak (surcharged) functions:
 126:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     examples HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback(), HAL_UART_RxHalfCpltCallback().
 127:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     Exception done for MspInit and MspDeInit functions that are respectively
 128:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     reset to the legacy weak (surcharged) functions in the HAL_UART_Init()
 129:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     and HAL_UART_DeInit() only when these callbacks are null (not registered beforehand).
 130:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     If not, MspInit or MspDeInit are not null, the HAL_UART_Init() and HAL_UART_DeInit()
 131:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     keep and use the user MspInit/MspDeInit callbacks (registered beforehand).
 132:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 133:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
 134:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     Callbacks can be registered/unregistered in HAL_UART_STATE_READY state only.
 135:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     Exception done MspInit/MspDeInit that can be registered/unregistered
 136:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     in HAL_UART_STATE_READY or HAL_UART_STATE_RESET state, thus registered (user)
 137:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     MspInit/DeInit callbacks can be used during the Init/DeInit.
 138:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     In that case first register the MspInit/MspDeInit user callbacks
 139:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     using HAL_UART_RegisterCallback() before calling HAL_UART_DeInit()
 140:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     or HAL_UART_Init() function.
 141:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 142:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..]
 143:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     When The compilation define USE_HAL_UART_REGISTER_CALLBACKS is set to 0 or
 144:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     not defined, the callback registration feature is not available
 145:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     and weak (surcharged) callbacks are used.
 146:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 147:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 148:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         Three operation modes are available within this driver :
 149:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 150:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      *** Polling mode IO operation ***
 151:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      =================================
 152:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 153:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Send an amount of data in blocking mode using HAL_UART_Transmit()
 154:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Receive an amount of data in blocking mode using HAL_UART_Receive()
 155:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 156:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      *** Interrupt mode IO operation ***
 157:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      ===================================
 158:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 159:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Send an amount of data in non blocking mode using HAL_UART_Transmit_IT()
 160:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) At transmission end of transfer HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback is executed and user can
 161:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback
 162:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Receive an amount of data in non blocking mode using HAL_UART_Receive_IT()
 163:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) At reception end of transfer HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback is executed and user can
 164:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback
 165:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) In case of transfer Error, HAL_UART_ErrorCallback() function is executed and user can
 166:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_ErrorCallback
 167:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 168:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      *** DMA mode IO operation ***
 169:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      ==============================
 170:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 171:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Send an amount of data in non blocking mode (DMA) using HAL_UART_Transmit_DMA()
 172:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) At transmission end of half transfer HAL_UART_TxHalfCpltCallback is executed and user ca
 173:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_TxHalfCpltCallback
 174:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) At transmission end of transfer HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback is executed and user can
 175:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_TxCpltCallback
 176:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Receive an amount of data in non blocking mode (DMA) using HAL_UART_Receive_DMA()
 177:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) At reception end of half transfer HAL_UART_RxHalfCpltCallback is executed and user can
 178:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_RxHalfCpltCallback
 179:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) At reception end of transfer HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback is executed and user can
 180:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_RxCpltCallback
 181:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) In case of transfer Error, HAL_UART_ErrorCallback() function is executed and user can
 182:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****             add his own code by customization of function pointer HAL_UART_ErrorCallback
 183:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Pause the DMA Transfer using HAL_UART_DMAPause()
 184:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Resume the DMA Transfer using HAL_UART_DMAResume()
 185:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Stop the DMA Transfer using HAL_UART_DMAStop()
 186:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 187:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 188:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     [..] This subsection also provides a set of additional functions providing enhanced reception
 189:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     services to user. (For example, these functions allow application to handle use cases
 190:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     where number of data to be received is unknown).
 191:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 192:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Compared to standard reception services which only consider number of received
 193:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         data elements as reception completion criteria, these functions also consider additional ev
 194:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         as triggers for updating reception status to caller :
 195:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Detection of inactivity period (RX line has not been active for a given period).
 196:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****           (++) RX inactivity detected by IDLE event, i.e. RX line has been in idle state (normally 
 197:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****                for 1 frame time, after last received byte.
 198:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 199:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) There are two mode of transfer:
 200:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Blocking mode: The reception is performed in polling mode, until either expected number 
 201:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            or till IDLE event occurs. Reception is handled only during function execution.
 202:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            When function exits, no data reception could occur. HAL status and number of actually re
 203:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            are returned by function after finishing transfer.
 204:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (+) Non-Blocking mode: The reception is performed using Interrupts or DMA.
 205:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            These API's return the HAL status.
 206:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The end of the data processing will be indicated through the
 207:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            dedicated UART IRQ when using Interrupt mode or the DMA IRQ when using DMA mode.
 208:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL_UARTEx_RxEventCallback() user callback will be executed during Receive process
 209:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            The HAL_UART_ErrorCallback()user callback will be executed when a reception error is det
 210:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 211:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Blocking mode API:
 212:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle()
 213:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 214:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API with Interrupt:
 215:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle_IT()
 216:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 217:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     (#) Non-Blocking mode API with DMA:
 218:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****         (+) HAL_UARTEx_ReceiveToIdle_DMA()
 219:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 220:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 221:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      *** UART HAL driver macros list ***
 222:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      =============================================
 223:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 224:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        Below the list of most used macros in UART HAL driver.
 225:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 226:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_ENABLE: Enable the UART peripheral
 227:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_DISABLE: Disable the UART peripheral
 228:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_GET_FLAG : Check whether the specified UART flag is set or not
 229:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_CLEAR_FLAG : Clear the specified UART pending flag
 230:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_ENABLE_IT: Enable the specified UART interrupt
 231:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_DISABLE_IT: Disable the specified UART interrupt
 232:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****       (+) __HAL_UART_GET_IT_SOURCE: Check whether the specified UART interrupt has occurred or not
 233:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 234:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 235:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (@) You can refer to the UART HAL driver header file for more useful macros
 236:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c **** 
 237:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****   @endverbatim
 238:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****      [..]
 239:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****        (@) Additional remark: If the parity is enabled, then the MSB bit of the data written
 240:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            in the data register is transmitted but is changed by the parity bit.
 241:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            Depending on the frame length defined by the M bit (8-bits or 9-bits),
 242:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****            the possible UART frame formats are as listed in the following table:
 243:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     +-------------------------------------------------------------+
 244:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |   M bit |  PCE bit  |            UART frame                 |
 245:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |---------------------|---------------------------------------|
 246:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |    0    |    0      |    | SB | 8 bit data | STB |          |
 247:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |---------|-----------|---------------------------------------|
 248:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |    0    |    1      |    | SB | 7 bit data | PB | STB |     |
 249:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |---------|-----------|---------------------------------------|
 250:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |    1    |    0      |    | SB | 9 bit data | STB |          |
 251:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |---------|-----------|---------------------------------------|
 252:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     |    1    |    1      |    | SB | 8 bit data | PB | STB |     |
 253:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****     +-------------------------------------------------------------+
 254:../hal/chipwhisperer-fw-extra/pinata/STM32F4xx_HAL_Driver/Src/stm32f4xx_hal_uart.c ****   ******************************************************************************
